{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 28, "model_name": "nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b", "content": "**Cherry Blossoms and City Lights: My Japan Adventure**\n\nLanding in Tokyo felt like stepping into a living postcard. The first morning I wandered through Ueno Park, where pink sakura petals fluttered like confetti against a backdrop of ancient temples and modern skyscrapers. Sipping matcha at a tiny tea stall, I watched locals practice tai chi, their movements as graceful as the falling blossoms.\n\nA quick Shinkansen ride whisked me to Kyoto, the heart of Japan’s tradition. I lost myself in the winding alleys of Gion, hoping to catch a glimpse of a geisha hurrying to an appointment. The Fushimi Inari Shrine greeted me with thousands of vermilion torii gates, each one a promise of discovery. Climbing the mountain trail, the air grew cooler, and the city’s hum faded into a serene whisper.\n\nEvenings were for food. In Osaka’s Dotonbori district, I devoured takoyaki hot off the grill, its octopus filling bursting with flavor, and later slurped steaming bowls of ramen in a tiny stall where the chef nodded approvingly at my enthusiastic slurps. Night markets glittered with neon signs, and the scent of yakitori drifted through the air, inviting me to try one more skewer.\n\nA day trip to Nara offered a gentle contrast: friendly deer bowed for crackers, and the towering Buddha at Tōdai‑ji reminded me of Japan’s deep spiritual roots. As my journey ended, I sat on a quiet bench overlooking Tokyo Bay, the skyline glittering like a sea of stars. Japan had woven together ancient serenity and pulsating energy into a tapestry I’ll carry home forever.", "logprobs": [{"token": "We", "logprob": -0.08967602252960205}, {"token": " need", "logprob": -0.0019025574438273907}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.05393047258257866}, {"token": " write", "logprob": -0.6954319477081299}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.0299712922424078}, {"token": " short", "logprob": -0.000